>> title: Pizza Dough
>> category: Breads
>> tags: bread, pizza, italian, yeast, dough
>> counters: Pizzeria
>> pairs-with: marinara-sauce
>> servings: 4
>> time: 27 hr
>> slack: forgiving — the dough cannot go into the fridge warm: one that has run away before it chills has spent its gluten and stretches into holes

>> step: whisk the dry mix
Whisk @bread flour{3 1/2%cup}(500 g), @instant yeast{1/2%tsp}(1.5 g), @fine sea salt{2%tsp}(12 g), and @granulated sugar{1%tsp}(4 g) together.

>> step: stir in
Stir @warm water{1 1/3%cup}(315 g) and @extra-virgin olive oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL) into @&(~1)dry mix{}.

>> step: knead 8 min until smooth
Knead @&(~1)shaggy dough{} for ~{8%min}.

>> step: cover, rise 2 hours
Cover @&(~1)dough{} and rise ~{2%hours}.

>> step: divide into four balls, oil, cold-ferment 24 hours
Divide @&(~1)dough{} into four balls, rub with @olive oil{2%tsp}(10 mL), and refrigerate ~{24%hours}.
